sub:assertion {
<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/levin-2015-girardia-18> a <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/Claim>;
    dc:description "The authors propose conceptualizing the link between gap junctional connectivity among planarian cells and discrete regenerative outcomes by viewing the cells as a neural-like network that processes developmental information more slowly but obeys the same statistical dynamics as the brain.";
    dc:type "conceptual";
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Somatic cells can be modeled as a slow neural-like network obeying brain-like dynamics";
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/context> "Emmons-Bell M, Durant F, Hammelman J, Bessonov N, Volpert V, Morokuma J, Pinet K, Adams DS, Pietak A, Lobo D, Levin M, “Gap Junctional Blockade Stochastically Induces Different Species-Specific Head Anatomies in Genetically Wild-Type Girardia dorotocephala Flatworms”, International journal of molecular sciences (2015), doi:10.3390/ijms161126065; section “3. Discussion › 3.7. A hypothesis: Physiological Network Attractors Underlie Regions of Anatomical Morphospace”. Scope: Planarian somatic cell networks during regeneration"
}
